@misc{CartonSudberyYassawi2026,
  author={Carton, Olivier and Sudbery, Jake and Yassawi, Reem},
  title={From some {Pisot} numerations to topological groups},
  year={2026}, eprint={2606.30496}, archivePrefix={arXiv},
  primaryClass={math.DS},
  month={Jun},
  note={Submitted 29 Jun 2026; 29 pages, PDF at
    \texttt{refs/FullText/arXiv\_2606.30496\_CartonSudberyYassawi2026\_
    Pisot-numerations-topological-groups.pdf} and full text at
    \texttt{refs/FullText/arXiv\_2606.30496\_CartonSudberyYassawi2026\_
    Pisot-numerations-topological-groups.txt}.
    Two pieces.  (i) Topology: for a Pisot numeration U satisfying
    the pseudo-valuation bound $\\nu_U(x+y) \ge \\min(\\nu_U(x),
    \\nu_U(y)) - K$ ("preserves zeros", equivalent to Frougny--
    Solomyak Condition F for $\\beta$-numerations), the construction
    $\\mathbb{Z}_U = G / H_U$ (where $G$ is bounded integer-valued
    sequences and $H_U$ is the closure of finite expansions of $0$)
    is a topological group carrying a continuous homomorphism
    $\\Phi: \\mathbb{Z}_U \\to \\mathbb{T}^{d-1}$ onto a torus; for
    unimodular Pisot U, $\\Phi$ is an isomorphism (Theorem 1.1).
    (ii) Automaton: the carry propagation for $g + h$ in $\\mathbb{Z}_U$
    is accepted by a finite deterministic automaton (after Messaoudi
    1998), and the homomorphic image factors through this automaton's
    state set.  Both pieces matter to this project: (i) makes the
    existing F-check (`include/adelic/coincidence_and_property_f.hpp`)
    the precondition for applying the topological iso to the unimodular
    Class-II $\\sigma_{a,1}$ family, and (ii) is exactly what
    `math/pisot_numeration_topology.hpp`'s `bifix_code` and `group_add`
    approximate; the integer-value carry we use is the homomorphic
    image of the automaton's exact carry, so $\\pi(a+b) = \\pi(a) +
    \\pi(b) \\bmod 1$ holds up to the finite-crossing correction
    recorded as a future obligation in the CSY test header.}}

