    tables for $\sigma_1$/$\sigma_2$ (a same-colour self-contact
    entry mistranscribed as a different colour pair in both examples;
    a dropped $-e_1$ term in $\sigma_2$'s list), found by computing
    the sets from the geometric definition rather than trusting the
    tables, plus a genuine notational ambiguity in the source's
    overloaded use of ``$-$'' for two different operations (triple-
    level swap-and-negate for node validity versus pair-level
    negate-only for the $\sim_r$ connection relation and hence the
    C-corona) that caused a real implementation bug (corona iteration
    diverging to 139 nodes instead of converging to 26) before being
    caught and fixed. Restated, corrected, and catalogued in
    \texttt{refs/loridant\_thuswaldner\_zhang\_2026\_corrected\_
    reference.tex} (self-authored working notes, not a copy of the
    source). This project's own \texttt{search\_D\_cont} computes
    $\mathfrak{D}_{\mathrm{cont}}$ from the geometric definition
    directly rather than transcribing the paper's tables, so it was
    never exposed to the transcription errors; \texttt{same\_letter\_H}
    in \texttt{include/ravel/corona.hpp} already implements the
    corrected pair-level ($\boxminus$) negation the source's C-corona
    definition actually needs, independently re-deriving the same fix
    the predecessor tree found. See \texttt{docs/LITERATURE_AUDIT_
    CLASS_II.md} for the cross-reference.}}

